## Why This Is Asked

Tests a complex, cross-origin integration scenario with iframe messaging, localStorage persistence, and multi-tenant isolation—common in partner ecosystems like Salesforce, Cloudflare, and Coinbase. It probes reliability under network blips and ensures data integrity across domains.

## Key Concepts

- Cross-origin messaging via postMessage between host and iframe
- Frame targeting with frameLocator/selectors
- Draft persistence in localStorage and autosave recovery
- Network fault injection and retry semantics
- Tenant data isolation across partner domains

## Code Example

```javascript
// Playwright sketch (conceptual only)
const host = page.locator('#host-app');
const frame = host.frameLocator('iframe#widget-form');
await frame.locator('input[name="name"]').fill('Acme Corp');
// simulate cross-origin event
await page.evaluate(() => {
  window.postMessage({type: 'INIT', tenant: 'tenantA'}, '*');
});
// flaky submit
await page.route('https://api.partner.com/submit', route => {
  route.fulfill({ status: 500, body: '{}' });
});
await frame.locator('button[type="submit"]').click();
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test race conditions between postMessage handlers across both domains?
- How would you validate that autosaved drafts don’t leak between tenants when the host cache is cleared?

